            "icon": "🌻",
            "cue": "loam"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So who likes sandy soil?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Cactus plants! They come from dry places. In sandy soil, rain runs away fast, so their roots stay dry.",
      "punch": "cactus",
      "board": {
        "type": "flow",
        "title": "Rain in sand",
        "packet": "💧",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🌧️",
            "label": "Rain",
            "cue": "rain"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🏖️",
            "label": "Sandy soil",
            "cue": "sandy"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⬇️",
            "label": "Runs away",
            "cue": "runs"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And who likes clay soil?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Rice loves lots of water! Farmers grow rice in flooded fields, and clay-like soil helps keep the water in.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌾",
        "text": "Rice likes wet fields",
        "cue": "rice",
        "sub": "Clay holds water",
        "sub_cue": "clay"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What about vegetables?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Lots of vegetables grow best in loam. It holds some water, drains the extra, and has plenty of humus.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "Loam has",
        "icon": "🥕",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Some water",
            "icon": "💧",
            "cue": "holds",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Drains extra",
            "icon": "⬇️",
            "cue": "drains",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Lots of humus",
            "icon": "🍂",
            "cue": "humus",
            "ok": true
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Do trees pick soil too?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Sort of! Pine trees can grow in sandy soil. Mangrove trees grow in wet, salty mud by the sea.",
